/** @defgroup bflat_ts_bcl_subst bflat build - substituted CoreLib methods
 * @ingroup bflat_ts
 * @{
 *
 * @brief Behavioral tests for the CoreLib surface that bflat's zisk modules
 *        replace or divert on the rv64ima (no-FPU) targets.
 *
 *        The zisk_subst module substitutes method bodies via
 *        ILLink.Substitutions and C# snippets (zisk.snippets.cs), and the
 *        rhp/pal modules divert symbols with --wrap. Each replacement must be
 *        semantics-preserving for every guest, so each one gets a test pinning
 *        the observable behavior:
 *        - System.Random compat impls: integer scaling of Next(max) /
 *          Next(min, max) for seeded and derived Random
 *        - System.Collections.Hashtable: integer load-factor ctors and rehash
 *        - ValueType.GetHashCode over float/double fields: raw bit-pattern
 *          hashing consistent with byte-wise ValueType.Equals
 *        - HashHelpers.IsPrime/GetPrime: integer reimplementation driving
 *          Dictionary/HashSet/Hashtable growth
 *        - Frozen collections: CalcNumBuckets wrap + LengthBuckets fallback
 *        - ArrayPool: trim gate stubbed to "memory pressure low"
 *        - Array.Copy/Buffer.BlockCopy fast paths (primitive widening removed)
 *        - Convert integer/string overloads (double overload removed)
 *        - Invariant TimeZoneInfo with stubbed transition math; integer
 *          DateTime/TimeSpan/Stopwatch tick arithmetic over wrapped
 *          clock_gettime
 *
 * @}
 */
